WEBVTT

00:00.580 --> 00:04.190
All right!
Let's start Hide-and-God-Seek!

00:04.190 --> 00:07.740
Wait a minute!

00:12.530 --> 00:13.390
Asta!

00:13.390 --> 00:16.160
Yes! Konoha! Kyrgis!
Hurry up!

00:16.160 --> 00:17.620
R-Right!

00:17.620 --> 00:18.780
Activating now!

00:26.910 --> 00:28.950
You didn't use your Arise?

00:28.950 --> 00:30.870
My Arise is that it won't let me die.

00:32.910 --> 00:34.010
Get out of here, Leshea!

00:35.220 --> 00:36.180
It's too dangerous to—

00:41.370 --> 00:42.400
What?

00:43.020 --> 00:45.140
That's the former god for you...

00:45.140 --> 00:50.810
This is not even my 100% power.
I can't use my god's power after all.

00:55.820 --> 00:58.930
You are surprisingly cute, Fay.

00:58.930 --> 01:01.580
And you seemed worried
about me earlier, didn't you?

01:05.270 --> 01:08.970
GODS' GAMES WE PLAY

01:10.510 --> 01:13.970
10 MINUTES AGO

01:14.600 --> 01:16.110
PLAYER.02: HIDE-AND-GOD-SEEK

01:16.110 --> 01:18.460
I haven't even said
I'd team up with you yet.

01:19.640 --> 01:24.930
Huh? We're definitely in Elements, right?
This place is just like our town.

01:26.130 --> 01:29.280
I can't really guess what
other gods might be thinking.

01:29.280 --> 01:32.130
There are many gods I don't know.

01:32.600 --> 01:34.370
Ah, right there!

01:34.370 --> 01:36.300
We never know what might happen...

01:37.220 --> 01:37.950
Fay?

01:38.450 --> 01:41.230
What's wrong? I heard you took
a leave of absence.

01:41.230 --> 01:43.420
Hello, Senior Asta.

01:43.800 --> 01:45.010
It's been a while.

01:45.010 --> 01:48.100
Actually, I just got back earlier,
and I sort of got dragged in here.

01:48.500 --> 01:50.260
Let's have a good game, guys.

01:50.260 --> 01:52.000
L-Lady Dragon God?!

01:52.000 --> 01:55.470
L-Lady Leoleshea?!
W-What are you doing here?!

01:55.470 --> 02:00.080
I'm participating in this game.
Don't worry, I'm on your side.

02:00.080 --> 02:02.490
Hello and welcome!

02:04.670 --> 02:08.150
Welcome to my Elements!

02:08.150 --> 02:12.980
My name is Meep, and I live in this realm
wherein lives my master, the God Titan.

02:12.980 --> 02:16.570
Since the time has come,
no further participants will be admitted.

02:16.940 --> 02:18.250
Send the video.

02:18.250 --> 02:18.970
Yes.

02:29.460 --> 02:33.540
Humanity's mission is to win
10 games against the gods.

02:33.930 --> 02:35.950
We're counting on you, Fay.

02:36.890 --> 02:40.160
Let's see, 18 players in total, right?

02:40.160 --> 02:43.050
Well then, let me introduce
the game for you!

02:43.050 --> 02:45.520
If this is against God Titan,
it's a battle game, right?

02:45.520 --> 02:48.750
The global statistics for
the last 30 years show that

02:48.750 --> 02:50.940
there have been 23 encounters
with the God Titan.

02:50.940 --> 02:55.440
And the win rate is 14% for our numbers.

02:55.440 --> 02:57.050
That works for me.

02:57.050 --> 03:00.740
If it's a battle game,
we have the Dragon God Leoleshea on our side.

03:00.740 --> 03:05.830
My deity, Lord Titan, says he is
tired of playing battle games.

03:07.580 --> 03:11.300
The game is,
Hide-and-God-Seek!

03:11.300 --> 03:14.050
I have never heard of such a game.

03:14.050 --> 03:17.090
Is it basically just hide-and-seek?

03:17.540 --> 03:20.560
We have to escape from Titan
in this group of buildings...

03:21.140 --> 03:23.350
Which, I guess, makes it
Hide-and-God-Seek instead.

03:23.950 --> 03:24.880
Am I wrong?

03:25.770 --> 03:27.850
That's exactly what it is!

03:28.170 --> 03:30.690
No one is allowed to go
beyond the border of light.

03:30.690 --> 03:35.730
You must run away from Lord Titan
inside this field.

03:35.730 --> 03:39.500
If this is a game of tag,
do we lose if we all get caught?

03:39.500 --> 03:42.290
That is one of the lose conditions.

03:43.060 --> 03:48.080
I see. Then there are other ways to lose
than everyone getting caught, right?

03:48.080 --> 03:52.020
It seems that our victory condition
is not so simple either.

03:52.820 --> 03:55.800
"Running away to win"
—but that's not enough, right?

03:56.100 --> 04:00.990
Correct! In this Hide-and-God-Seek,
you have to keep running away to win,

04:00.990 --> 04:03.690
but you can lose even if
you escape safely.

04:03.690 --> 04:05.630
That's all for the rule explanation!

04:05.630 --> 04:09.650
By the way, you have 300 seconds
head start to start hiding!

04:09.650 --> 04:10.380
WIN CONDITION

04:10.380 --> 04:11.130
?????

04:11.130 --> 04:11.850
LOSE CONDITION 1

04:11.850 --> 04:12.640
ALL PLAYERS ARE GETTING CAUGHT BY TITAN

04:12.640 --> 04:13.280
LOSE CONDITION 2

04:13.280 --> 04:13.950
?????

04:13.950 --> 04:14.650
(PLAYERS MAY STILL LOSE EVEN IF THEY ESCAPE)

04:19.810 --> 04:20.820
What?

04:20.820 --> 04:24.600
Oops? It seems Lord Titan
can't wait any longer.

04:24.600 --> 04:27.440
So there is no head start!

04:27.440 --> 04:28.660
What?!

04:31.000 --> 04:34.890
Wait a minute!

04:38.380 --> 04:41.260
PRESENT

04:49.350 --> 04:50.940
I-It's so fast!

04:50.940 --> 04:52.400
Captain, we can't keep this up!

04:52.400 --> 04:55.570
Even if we have Superhuman speed,
we can't get away from him!

04:55.920 --> 04:57.190
How about using flying magic?

04:57.190 --> 04:59.280
N-No, it's still impossible!

04:59.280 --> 05:02.760
Scatter! Split up and hide
behind the buildings!

05:02.760 --> 05:03.600
Roger!

05:10.200 --> 05:12.740
I don't think I'm going
to have much to do here.

05:12.740 --> 05:14.870
They might call this a game of tag,

05:14.870 --> 05:17.860
but it's more like
hide-and-seek, don't you think?

05:17.860 --> 05:20.050
I think we should hide in the building.

05:20.050 --> 05:24.260
T-That's a good plan, Vice Captain!
Titan might not notice us if we hide!

05:24.610 --> 05:26.680
That's a bad idea!
Don't do it, Senior Asta!

05:27.430 --> 05:28.320
Huh?

05:28.860 --> 05:30.210
Why?

05:32.890 --> 05:36.530
He's got a vague idea of where we are.

05:37.730 --> 05:39.220
Watch out, Senior Asta!

05:40.610 --> 05:42.820
Asta! Run towards us, now!

06:00.050 --> 06:02.130
Shouldn't it already be game over for me?

06:05.780 --> 06:08.960
N-No! What's going on?!

06:11.270 --> 06:13.310
Huh? My magic is moving on its own...?

06:16.420 --> 06:18.190
Asta, have you gone insane?!

06:18.190 --> 06:22.780
N-No, you're wrong!
My magic comes out on its own!

06:23.180 --> 06:26.120
So Hide-and-God-Seek
was more than just a name.

06:26.120 --> 06:26.960
HIDDEN RULE 1:

06:26.960 --> 06:28.220
THOSE WHO ARE IMMOBILIZED BY GOD'S ATTACK
Of course, they have prepared

06:28.220 --> 06:30.190
BECOME GOD'S SERVANTS
hidden rules, right?

06:30.190 --> 06:32.710
BECOME GOD'S SERVANTS
It's a game of wits with the gods!

06:32.710 --> 06:34.920
Run away, Vice Captain!

06:34.920 --> 06:38.500
Is that what you say
while firing wind magic at us?!

06:44.300 --> 06:45.760
C-Crap!

06:56.900 --> 06:58.430
N-No way!

06:58.430 --> 07:00.860
The Titan didn't even touch us!

07:00.860 --> 07:03.130
What's wrong with
the definition of touch here?

07:03.130 --> 07:04.880
I think we might be in trouble, too.

07:04.880 --> 07:06.910
Yeah! We must go!

07:08.740 --> 07:10.910
That makes four apostles on god's side.

07:10.910 --> 07:12.910
Five if you count the Titan.

07:13.500 --> 07:16.000
HUMAN VS GOD
14 - 5

07:26.020 --> 07:27.850
He didn't come after us?

07:27.850 --> 07:29.370
Is he changing directions?

07:34.390 --> 07:38.590
If he can take out everyone but us,
it'll be 2 versus 17 on god's side.

07:38.590 --> 07:40.980
And he is going to attack us
with that gap in strength.

07:41.370 --> 07:44.680
Until then, he's going to let
his servants take care of it.

07:45.250 --> 07:50.110
I mean, her lower half of her body hasn't
changed color. It's just unbalanced.

07:50.110 --> 07:54.660
Shut up! My body
is chasing you on its own!

07:54.660 --> 07:57.810
Senior Asta was not game over yet.

07:57.810 --> 08:02.130
That's right. If she failed, she should
return to the human world unharmed.

08:02.130 --> 08:05.750
This game still has hidden rules, doesn't it?

08:05.750 --> 08:08.090
Even if she's going to be dyed
the same color as Titan,

08:08.410 --> 08:10.550
why only the upper half of her body?

08:29.300 --> 08:30.810
Hey! What is this?!

08:30.810 --> 08:31.620
Leshea!

08:32.630 --> 08:33.280
Hup.

08:34.580 --> 08:36.850
That was a successful touch.

08:36.850 --> 08:38.420
Now you're back on the human side.

08:38.420 --> 08:39.750
Huh?

08:46.780 --> 08:49.070
I'm back?

08:49.070 --> 08:54.050
It wasn't game over for you, senior.
Because your lower body didn't change color.

08:54.050 --> 08:54.960
HIDDEN RULE 2:

08:54.960 --> 08:57.310
BY TOUCHING ONE OF TITAN'S SERVANTS,
THEY CAN BE RETURNED TO THE HUMAN SIDE

08:57.310 --> 09:01.060
That means there must be a hidden rule
that we can bring people to the human side.

09:01.060 --> 09:02.610
I-I see!

09:06.970 --> 09:10.200
Oh no, he's going to chase us again.

09:10.200 --> 09:14.210
Now that we figured out this game,
he won't let us escape, huh?

09:14.210 --> 09:15.900
You must hide, Senior Asta!

09:15.900 --> 09:16.890
Got it!

09:22.080 --> 09:26.830
Titan is saying he's glad
you figured out his game, Fay.

09:34.040 --> 09:38.060
How can we win when
all we do is run away?

09:38.060 --> 09:40.140
Meep said it from the beginning:

09:40.140 --> 09:43.150
"Even if you keep running away,
you may still lose the game."

09:43.150 --> 09:45.120
WIN CONDITION
Figuring out how to win

09:45.120 --> 09:46.480
WIN CONDITION
is part of the game, huh?

09:46.480 --> 09:48.450
WIN CONDITION
It's different from a battle game

09:48.450 --> 09:51.610
WIN CONDITION
where we have to defeat the Titan.

09:51.610 --> 09:54.500
If we escape for a certain
amount of time, do we win?

09:54.500 --> 09:57.200
It is possible, but we don't have any proof.

09:57.580 --> 10:01.850
There's nothing suggesting how long
we have to keep running, either. Then...

10:06.040 --> 10:08.060
You're exactly what I expected!

10:08.060 --> 10:08.880
About what?

10:09.290 --> 10:14.340
We can talk to each other,
and you get what I'm trying to say.

10:14.340 --> 10:17.320
And more importantly, you put your
whole heart into playing the game.

10:17.320 --> 10:19.340
Huh? Isn't that obvious?

10:19.820 --> 10:22.430
It's a thrilling game, after all.

10:24.500 --> 10:28.400
That's what makes me happy.
I'm a former god myself.

10:28.400 --> 10:32.490
Games are fun when there are
humans who are willing

10:33.160 --> 10:34.990
to seriously play the gods' games.

10:42.500 --> 10:45.250
GAMES ARE MEANT TO BE FUN

10:48.210 --> 10:52.450
But I want to win for sure,
because it's so frustrating to lose.

10:52.450 --> 10:54.130
Of course!

10:54.130 --> 10:56.430
What are our winning conditions?

10:56.430 --> 10:58.890
There must be a hint for us at this point.

11:08.270 --> 11:11.610
I'm sorry.
We were wiped out.

11:11.610 --> 11:14.070
Yeah, I can see it.

11:14.070 --> 11:19.910
But you must not give up!
You two must escape!

11:21.650 --> 11:23.330
Then you could just let us go!

11:23.880 --> 11:26.250
My legs are moving on their own!

11:29.080 --> 11:30.190
Over here!

11:31.880 --> 11:34.050
HUMAN VS GOD
3 - 16

11:43.890 --> 11:46.430
We can buy time for a few
dozen seconds at most.

11:46.430 --> 11:48.850
Yeah. Let's hurry!

11:53.600 --> 11:57.910
So this is where the hidden rule about
becoming Titan's servant comes in.

11:57.910 --> 12:01.540
If it's the same people,
they can come after us. And now...

12:03.630 --> 12:05.040
The Titan is coming too.

12:05.040 --> 12:07.400
We're trapped with no way of escape.

12:07.400 --> 12:11.630
Just escaping is a problem, and we still
don't know the win condition of this game.

12:11.980 --> 12:16.510
I wish we had more people on our side.
And Asta is still hiding.

12:16.980 --> 12:22.220
The rest of us are all but wiped out.
They've all turned over to Titan's side now.

12:22.680 --> 12:23.720
So that's it...

12:24.140 --> 12:25.310
What's wrong?

12:25.310 --> 12:27.750
That's right, Leshea!
They've all turned over!

12:28.540 --> 12:29.980
Turn over?

12:29.980 --> 12:35.130
I knew it. There was a third game
in this "Hide-and-God-Seek"!

12:35.990 --> 12:38.990
GODS' GAMES WE PLAY

12:40.110 --> 12:41.450
This "Hide-and-God-Seek"

12:41.450 --> 12:46.770
was a combination of tag, hide-and-seek,
and the third game in there.

12:46.770 --> 12:49.190
Turn over... The third game...

12:49.750 --> 12:50.790
I see!

12:51.540 --> 12:55.100
That would explain
why there are two lose conditions!

12:55.100 --> 12:57.150
Then, let's split up!

13:02.970 --> 13:04.470
I'll take eight of them.

13:04.470 --> 13:06.310
No, seven is the right number.

13:06.310 --> 13:09.020
You're right.
I'll draw them out.

13:09.020 --> 13:10.310
And I'll go up.

13:28.630 --> 13:29.960
Titan, huh?

13:29.960 --> 13:32.920
So he's going to destroy the surrounding
buildings one after the other

13:32.920 --> 13:35.880
and finally destroy this
department store to checkmate.

13:36.420 --> 13:40.340
Please let us make it in time!
For me and Leshea!

13:50.310 --> 13:55.690
He used the apostles, under his command,
to lead me to the rooftop.

13:58.480 --> 14:01.110
To make sure he's the one
who finishes me, huh?

14:09.370 --> 14:10.660
He got him...

14:14.630 --> 14:15.670
HUMAN VS GOD
3 - 16

14:15.670 --> 14:17.210
HUMAN VS GOD
2 - 17

14:28.170 --> 14:31.850
The game ends when you
destroy all the buildings. Right?

14:33.420 --> 14:35.270
Even under the rules of Hide-and-God-Seek,

14:35.650 --> 14:39.480
I'm not being immobilized by your attack,
and I'm not under your control.

14:41.300 --> 14:44.780
Erasing all wounds and damage,
even the god's attack,

14:44.780 --> 14:46.450
the ultimate regeneration.

14:47.060 --> 14:48.530
My Arise is...

14:49.490 --> 14:50.880
"May Your God"!

14:52.090 --> 14:53.580
HUMAN VS GOD: 2 - 17
You think it doesn't matter

14:53.580 --> 14:57.040
HUMAN VS GOD: 3 - 16
if I come back because it's 3 vs 16, right?

14:57.560 --> 15:01.860
It's the opposite. We're the ones
who fulfilled the win condition, Titan!

15:03.310 --> 15:05.390
It's time to compare answers.

15:05.390 --> 15:08.470
The game that's been hidden under
Hide-and-God-Seek this entire time...

15:09.000 --> 15:10.200
...is reversi!

15:10.680 --> 15:14.730
It's made to look like a game of tag,
but this city is the game board, right?

15:15.280 --> 15:17.690
The god chases, and the people run.

15:18.230 --> 15:21.600
People become god's servants,
and other people rescue them.

15:22.070 --> 15:25.900
This is clearly made up of 'god is moving
first' and 'humans move second.'

15:26.270 --> 15:31.110
And when the people touch the upper half of
the servant's body, they've been turned over.

15:31.620 --> 15:33.580
This is the biggest hint of all.

15:34.040 --> 15:35.990
Each side took alternating turns.

15:35.990 --> 15:38.460
The color changes
when turned over by touching.

15:38.460 --> 15:41.300
Reversi satisfies these two conditions!

15:41.680 --> 15:43.760
Your Meep is excellent.

15:44.720 --> 15:46.970
The rule explanation
was the hint to this game.

15:48.800 --> 15:52.390
The game is on a square field.

15:52.390 --> 15:55.990
The game of reversi ended
when the board was full.

15:55.990 --> 16:00.860
In Hide-and-God-Seek, the game concludes
when the field is destroyed.

16:00.860 --> 16:05.070
The rest of the game is decided by
who has more pieces on their side.

16:05.070 --> 16:09.320
We had one thin ray of hope
for turning this all around.

16:09.840 --> 16:11.910
That is 'chaining.'

16:11.910 --> 16:15.000
When Senior Asta and the Vice Captain
were touched by Titan,

16:15.720 --> 16:18.220
the apostles nearby had turned over, too.

16:18.220 --> 16:22.250
At that time, Senior Asta slammed
the three apostles against the wall

16:22.590 --> 16:25.840
to line them up between her and Titan.

16:25.840 --> 16:29.050
So, the two in between
were flipped over to god's side.

16:29.980 --> 16:33.640
And my aim is to lure you.

16:33.640 --> 16:36.670
I'm going to use the same trick now!

16:37.600 --> 16:38.940
Senior Asta!

16:38.940 --> 16:42.520
Geez, Fay.
You're overworking your senior!

16:46.410 --> 16:47.280
Leshea!

16:53.780 --> 16:57.000
And then it all turns upside down!

17:02.920 --> 17:03.340
HIDDEN RULE 3

17:03.340 --> 17:03.980
WHEN RULES 1 AND 2 ARE FULFILLED,

17:03.980 --> 17:04.840
OPPONENT'S PIECES THAT ARE "SANDWICHED"
The seven people sandwiched between

17:04.840 --> 17:05.990
WILL CHAIN TOGETHER
The seven people sandwiched between

17:06.160 --> 17:07.510
HUMAN VS GOD: 3 - 16
Leshea and Senior Asta are turned over

17:07.510 --> 17:09.300
HUMAN VS GOD: 10 - 9
to the human's side in a chain reaction,

17:09.840 --> 17:12.160
and the game is set when
the whole building collapses.

17:12.160 --> 17:12.510
and the game is set when
the whole building collapses.
Human 10, God 9. We win.
Any objections?

17:12.510 --> 17:17.220
Human 10, God 9. We win.
Any objections?

17:34.700 --> 17:35.770
None...

17:36.740 --> 17:37.400
VS TITAN, THE SAGE OF THE EARTH

17:37.400 --> 17:40.710
HIDE-AND-GOD-SEEK
TIME ELAPSED: 3 HOURS, 31 MINUTES

17:40.710 --> 17:41.750
WIN

17:41.750 --> 17:42.290
WIN CONDITION:

17:42.290 --> 17:43.710
THE WHITE (HUMAN SIDE) HAS MORE PIECES THAN
THE BLACK (GOD SIDE) AT THE END OF THE GAME

17:43.710 --> 17:44.450
LOSE CONDITION 1:

17:44.450 --> 17:46.300
ALL PLAYERS ARE GETTING CAUGHT BY TITAN

17:46.300 --> 17:47.240
LOSE CONDITION 2:

17:47.240 --> 17:49.260
THE BLACK (GOD SIDE) HAS MORE PIECES THAN
THE WHITE (HUMAN SIDE) AT THE END OF THE GAME

17:49.260 --> 17:49.810
HIDDEN RULE 1:

17:49.810 --> 17:51.310
THOSE WHO ARE IMMOBILIZED BY GOD'S
ATTACK BECOME GOD'S SERVANTS

17:51.310 --> 17:51.780
HIDDEN RULE 2:

17:51.780 --> 17:53.250
BY TOUCHING ONE OF TITAN'S SERVANTS,
THEY CAN BE RETURNED TO THE HUMAN SIDE

17:53.250 --> 17:53.610
HIDDEN RULE 3:

17:53.610 --> 17:55.260
WHEN RULES 1 AND 2 ARE FULFILLED, OPPONENT'S
PIECES THAT ARE "SANDWICHED" WILL CHAIN TOGETHER

17:56.500 --> 17:59.980
It had been a full 35 days since
humanity last claimed victory.

17:59.980 --> 18:02.960
Yesterday, we had high global
viewership all over the world.

18:02.960 --> 18:06.270
In this city alone,
the ratings were over 70%.

18:06.270 --> 18:07.320
Was it really that big?

18:07.730 --> 18:09.520
We're raking it in, thanks to you.

18:10.010 --> 18:13.320
With the proceeds, we need all the apostles
we've trained to do their best

18:13.320 --> 18:16.250
and win the gods' game.

18:17.310 --> 18:21.590
So, how was it teaming up
with Lady Leoleshea?

18:21.590 --> 18:22.750
What do you mean?

18:22.750 --> 18:24.790
You two worked perfectly together.

18:24.790 --> 18:27.270
It's hard to believe that you two
were an impromptu team.

18:28.730 --> 18:29.710
What's wrong?

18:29.710 --> 18:32.110
To be honest, it was amazing.

18:32.110 --> 18:35.010
We can understand each other
with a quick glance.

18:35.010 --> 18:37.180
I guess she really is a former god.

18:37.760 --> 18:39.600
I'm sure I quite agree.

18:40.520 --> 18:42.390
It's not because she's a former god.

18:42.830 --> 18:47.730
I think it's because the team
was you and Lady Leoleshea.

18:50.180 --> 18:55.400
Lady Leoleshea had been playing
by herself before you got here.

18:55.400 --> 18:56.530
By herself?

18:57.070 --> 18:59.830
She was too strong.
That's why she had no partner.

18:59.830 --> 19:02.540
Not cards, not Go, not roulette.

19:03.280 --> 19:05.540
Alone, huh?

19:10.020 --> 19:12.260
I'm sure you'll be a great team.

19:12.650 --> 19:18.000
And it'll get you one step closer
to your wish to conquer the gods' game.

19:18.570 --> 19:20.150
I'll do my best.

19:26.360 --> 19:28.370
That's why I came back.

19:31.970 --> 19:33.780
Leshea, can I come in?

19:34.190 --> 19:35.330
Sure.

19:41.200 --> 19:44.760
Here, we ran into the department store,

19:44.760 --> 19:49.050
but I thought we could have taken
a left turn and gone into the cul-de-sac.

19:49.050 --> 19:50.960
Were you doing an evaluation?

19:50.960 --> 19:54.850
Well, that's enough.
I've seen it four times already.

19:54.850 --> 19:56.370
That many?!

19:56.370 --> 19:59.260
Hey. What's your wish?

19:59.260 --> 20:00.180
What?

20:00.180 --> 20:03.690
You know, a reward for winning
10 games against gods.

20:03.690 --> 20:07.340
Like me, I wish I could
go back to being a god.

20:10.580 --> 20:11.790
I do have a wish.

20:11.790 --> 20:13.820
What's your wish? Tell me!

20:14.630 --> 20:16.550
There's someone I want to find.

20:16.550 --> 20:17.690
Who?

20:17.690 --> 20:21.740
Someone who used to play games
with me when I was a kid.

20:22.240 --> 20:25.450
I never knew her name,
so I just called her "Sis."

20:26.170 --> 20:28.340
She taught me everything about the game.

20:28.790 --> 20:31.880
I was so young that I couldn't win
no matter how many times I tried,

20:31.880 --> 20:34.170
and I kept challenging
her morning and night,

20:34.580 --> 20:36.810
but she accepted everything with a smile.

20:37.670 --> 20:41.000
But one day, she just disappeared.

20:41.470 --> 20:44.160
She only promised me
that we would meet again.

20:44.560 --> 20:46.010
Sis!

20:50.340 --> 20:51.810
That's strange.

20:51.810 --> 20:56.210
I guess you could call her my mentor.
I just wanted to see her and say thank you.

20:56.210 --> 21:00.360
I am who I am today because of her.

21:00.360 --> 21:01.830
I see.

21:01.830 --> 21:07.500
I only have one wish: "Please find
that person I used to play with."

21:07.500 --> 21:09.850
That's an interesting request.

21:10.310 --> 21:14.340
But Fay, don't you have
any clue who that person is?

21:14.340 --> 21:16.090
Other than she likes to play games.

21:16.090 --> 21:20.290
I don't know her name, and I only have
a hazy memory of her voice and her face.

21:20.910 --> 21:22.800
But the only thing I remember

21:23.910 --> 21:28.220
is that she had vermilion-colored
hair just like yours.

21:29.270 --> 21:33.900
I wondered if you and Sis
were related in some way.

21:39.040 --> 21:42.240
I was trapped in a glacier
for 3,000 years, you know.

21:45.520 --> 21:46.580
That's true...

21:47.170 --> 21:49.040
But I hope your wish comes true.

21:51.550 --> 21:53.080
Let's team up and make it happen.

21:54.470 --> 21:58.410
Maybe it's fate that I met Leshea,
who looks exactly like Sis.

21:58.800 --> 22:04.110
Yeah. I promise,
I'll play with all my strength.

22:04.110 --> 22:07.510
I promise we can clear those
10 games in god's game.
